From: Alysander Stanley <alysander@vivi.io>
Date: Tue, 30 Sep 2026 20:40:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] tcp-passive: bind the listener with address reuse

A tcp-passive host candidate listens on the agent's port range. When the
previous connection on that port is still in TIME_WAIT, a bind without
SO_REUSEADDR fails with EADDRINUSE, and with a one-port range the whole
gather fails and every candidate is freed. Binding with reuse lets the
listener take a port whose last connection is in TIME_WAIT; a port with
a live listener still refuses.
---
 socket/tcp-passive.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/socket/tcp-passive.c b/socket/tcp-passive.c
--- a/socket/tcp-passive.c
+++ b/socket/tcp-passive.c
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@
   /* GSocket: All socket file descriptors are set to be close-on-exec. */
   g_socket_set_blocking (gsock, false);
 
-  gret = g_socket_bind (gsock, gaddr, FALSE, error) &&
+  gret = g_socket_bind (gsock, gaddr, TRUE, error) &&
       g_socket_listen (gsock, error);
   g_object_unref (gaddr);
 
